ShortDescription: Local-first public identifier observability with explainable evidence
Description: >-
  SocialName searches whether a public identifier exists on supported sites and
  shows the evidence behind every answer: the evidence class, the matcher
  outcome, the exact rule identity, and when the measurement was taken. The
  desktop application runs locally by default with no account and no
  synchronization. A matching username across sites is not proof that the
  accounts belong to one person, and this build reports ten representative
  sites whose rules have not yet passed their live validation gate.
